  "title": "Per-lens answer schema for reviewer runs",
  "summary": "Reviewer runs previously handed every agent the same static review-answer schema, whose `scores` object was unconstrained. This change adds `answer::schema_for(lens)`, which clones the compiled-in schema and rewrites `properties.scores` into a closed object with one required numeric property per criterion of the lens being run. `reviewers::run_with_retry` now builds that schema once per run and threads it through `run_child` and `build_args`, so both the schema file written for path-style reviewers and the inlined schema value carry the lens-specific criteria. Tests assert the generated schema obeys the structured-output keyword rules for every shipped lens and that a real codex answer validates against it.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
